    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **284 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreation.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`.\n- Reads the authenticated user from Spring Security's `SecurityContextHolder`.\n- Records the user, the new owner's `id`, and its `membershipNumber`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` (where the id is generated) and `respond`, so it only runs after a successful save.\n\nThe step runs after `SaveOwner` so the owner id is populated (`@Val Owner` yields the same saved entity). The new `Cp19Tests` acceptance test passes, confirming the AUDIT logger emits a message containing `acceptance-admin` and the owner id (`Owner created by user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`), and no existing tests regressed.",
